# ws/sd-3k — a bounded spin-then-sleep doorbell for the 3k-row fetch
#
# One change on top of merge/transport (303366d): the shm engine's waits are a
# bounded spin on the sequence counter before the semaphore sleep. A small
# batch's partner is normally still running when the handoff is posted, so the
# spin catches the answer and the futex sleep/wake drops out of the critical
# path. Anything longer falls through to sem_timedwait exactly as before. The
# spin is skipped above 16384 rows (FASTPOSTGRES_SPIN_MAX_BATCH), where the
# partner's turn is milliseconds and the sleep is the cheaper wait; it can be
# disabled entirely with FASTPOSTGRES_SPIN_US=0.
#
# Where the per-fetch cost actually is (measured, not assumed): with the worker
# instrumented at 3000 rows/fetch, `ring.next_rows()` is 261.3 us of worker wall
# per fetch, of which PortalRunFetch is 259.1 us (99.2%). SPI connect/find/finish
# is 0.5 us, the cursor name and segment path 0.4 us, the segment-map cache hit
# 0.0 us, the per-batch context/arrays 0.2 us, the column headers 1.1 us and the
# publish 0.0 us. The map-cache workstream already removed the mapping cost, so
# the only remaining fixed cost outside the executor is the doorbell: the
# driver's worker wall is ~294 us at 3k against those 261 us inside the worker.
# That is the slice this change takes.
#
# Command (run once per side, alternating, one at a time under /tmp/fpq-bench.lock;
# the driver is bind-mounted so every image runs the identical file):
#
#   docker build -q --target dev -t fpq-<side> -f docker/Dockerfile .
#   docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=<side> \
#     -v $PWD/bench/dispatch/worker-map-batch.py:/src/bench/dispatch/worker-map-batch.py:ro \
#     fpq-<side> python3 /src/bench/dispatch/worker-map-batch.py 3000 100
#
# and the 100K control, three to eight runs per side:
#
#   docker run --rm --shm-size=3g -e BENCH_GIT_REV=<side> fpq-<side> benchmarks.sh 100000
#
# Sides:
#   baseline  fpq-baseline      main@7e3d2e6
#   base      fpq-sd-3k-base    merge/transport @ 303366d (the tree this branch builds on)
#   change    fpq-sd-3k         this branch
#
# The baseline -> change row is the protocol A/B (the cumulative merge plus this
# change); base -> change is the incremental A/B for this slice alone. Five
# interleaved runs per 3k side, eight per 100k base/change side (three for the
# baseline). Medians quoted; raw values below them.

### ENV
cpu: AMD Ryzen 7 7700 8-Core Processor
mem: 30 GiB
ghz: 3.8
cores: 8
postgres: 18.6
python: 3.13.5
sqlalchemy: 2.0.40
pyarrow: 26.0.0
adbc: 1.13.0
shape: bench
shm: 3.0G
### END ENV

