# zero-copy:  9.52 9.15 8.69 8.69 8.85 9.24 8.96 9.28  -> median 9.05M

### change (ws/sd-3k, 8 runs)
# DBAPI raw:  7.71 7.71 7.77 7.81 7.55 7.36 8.08 7.65  -> median 7.71M
# stream raw: 8.79 9.12 9.03 8.91 8.97 8.86 8.90 8.34  -> median 8.91M
# 4 procs:    23.50 23.66 23.99 23.30 23.49 23.14 23.76 22.99 -> median 23.49M
# zero-copy:  8.19 8.66 8.92 9.13 8.79 8.85 8.89 8.47  -> median 8.82M

### AB (100K rows/fetch)
# baseline -> change: DBAPI 3.72M -> 7.71M (+107.3%), stream() 8.32M -> 8.91M (+7.0%),
#                     4 procs 8.62M -> 23.49M (+172.6%)  [the cumulative merge]
# base -> change:     DBAPI 7.70M -> 7.71M (+0.1%), stream() 9.08M -> 8.91M (-1.9%),
#                     4 procs 23.83M -> 23.49M (-1.4%), zero-copy 9.05M -> 8.82M (-2.6%)
# The batch is 100000, so FASTPOSTGRES_SPIN_MAX_BATCH (16384) skips the spin and
# the hot path is the base's; the small non-DBAPI deltas are inside the harness'
# documented +/-5-10% run-to-run spread (the base's own DBAPI runs span 7.02-8.46M).
# The 100K control does not move.

## worker-internal breakdown at 3k (instrumentation run, base image)
# FPROF calls=101 next_total=261.3 us/fetch connect=0.1 name=0.2 find=0.1 path=0.2 rows=260.9 finish=0.1
# FPROF rows: map=0.0 ctx=0.2 arr=0.0 hdr=1.1 fetch=259.1 pub=0.0 free=0.0 us/fetch
# -> SPI + cursor-name/path + map cache + per-batch context/arrays + headers + publish
#    together are 2.2 us of 261.3. Reusing a cursor or its buffers cannot pay for
#    itself; the spin doorbell is the remaining reducible fixed cost.

